Bridge 0133 (U12-1b): react to a GPU restart that dropped this process's work. Turnip 0112 keeps the VkDevice after the kernel
recovered a hung GPU; the kernel drops all work in flight and forces its fences done, so dropped work looked Completed and one-time
uploads stayed wrong. 0112 exports tu_darwin_restarts() (status checks that found work dropped; run inside every vkWaitForFences and
vkWaitSemaphores), found once by dlsym (global, else the loaded libvulkan_freedreno.dylib, as creation_log.rs finds MoltenVK's
statistics).
- Waited copies (device/submit.rs submit_internal: host copies, staged texel copies, readbacks, mipmaps; device/staging.rs, unused on
  Adreno: one queue family) snapshot the count and the queues' use count (QueueSlot::with, counted under the queue lock) as they go.
  If the count moved once the fence signalled, the copy's own command buffer (not one-time while the count is read) goes once more
  while what it reads is held, never the first-work buffer (PREINITIALIZED/foreign moves, zero fills: not valid to replay), and
  only if no queue was used since (checked under queue 0's lock for submit_internal). Within 60 s of a redo whose own flight saw
  another restart, no redo is made.
- Command buffers: each batch snapshots the count as it is submitted; a batch that completes with the count moved marks its command
  buffer, which finishes with CommandBufferError::Execution(1), "Discarded (victim of GPU error/recovery)" (Metal's error for a
  recovery victim). The frontend (in place, NativeBridgeMetalFrontend.mm + bridge/NativeMetalObjects.rs/.h,
  nmb_command_buffer_execution_code) answers an Execution failure as MTLCommandBufferErrorDomain with its code
  (1 = MTLCommandBufferErrorInternal). CoreAnimation's completion handler only logs a command buffer error.
Not covered: staged byte copies and first work (in the first-work buffer, or carried by an app batch) are not redone.
Off: SWEET_RESTART_REDO=0 (or a Turnip without 0112). Log: "MTL2[pid prog]: GPU restart: redid N staging copies, M command buffers
marked error (restarts R)" (process totals) plus "; redo skipped: newer work on the queue", "; redo skipped: within 60 s of a redo
that saw another restart" or "; another restart in the redo's flight: redos held 60 s".

